---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const capabilities = [
  ['Repository Intelligence', 'Build a structural view of repositories, files, symbols, and relationships.'],
  ['Dependency Intelligence', 'Trace dependencies and connected components to understand change surface.'],
  ['Change Intelligence', 'Connect code changes to affected areas and engineering risk signals.'],
  ['PR Intelligence', 'Turn pull-request changes into structured impact and review context.'],
  ['Architecture Intelligence', 'Surface architectural relationships and boundary concerns from repository evidence.'],
  ['Grounded Evidence', 'Keep engineering conclusions tied to identifiable repository evidence.'],
  ['Repository Q&A', 'Ask questions against repository context rather than relying only on generic model knowledge.'],
  ['Engineering Planner', 'Produce structured, evidence-backed implementation plans before code changes.']
];
---

<BaseLayout title="CodeContext — Evidence-driven engineering intelligence" description="Understand repositories, dependencies, changes, architecture, and engineering plans with evidence-backed context.">
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> Engineering intelligence for real repositories</div>
    <h1>Understand the codebase<br /><span>before changing it.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">CodeContext turns repository structure, dependencies, history, architecture, and changes into grounded engineering context for developers and teams.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/CodeContext">View on GitHub ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="#demo">Explore the proof</a></div>
    <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example CodeContext analysis output"><div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><strong>codecontext analysis</strong></div><pre><code><span class="dim">$</span> codecontext analyze ./payment-service

<span class="ok">✓</span> Repository indexed             <b>428 files</b>
<span class="ok">✓</span> Dependency relationships        <b>1,284</b>
<span class="ok">✓</span> Architecture boundaries         <b>12</b>
<span class="warn">△</span> High-impact change surface      <b>3 components</b>

<span class="accent">Evidence</span>
  E17  PaymentService → PaymentRepository
  E21  PaymentController → PaymentService
  E34  recent change touches fraud flow

<span class="accent">Plan</span>
  01  inspect affected contracts
  02  update implementation
  03  verify impacted tests</code></pre></div>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">01 / CAPABILITIES</span><h2>From repository structure to engineering context.</h2><p>Current CodeContext capabilities, presented from the implementation rather than marketing assumptions.</p></div><div class="capability-grid">{capabilities.map(([title, description], index) => (<article class="capability-card"><span class="index">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>))}</div></section>

  <section id="architecture" class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">02 / ARCHITECTURE</span><h2>Evidence first. Reasoning second.</h2><p>CodeContext is designed so deterministic repository analysis can provide the factual foundation for higher-level engineering workflows.</p></div><div class="flow" aria-label="CodeContext processing flow"><div>Repository</div><i>→</i><div>Analysis</div><i>→</i><div>Evidence</div><i>→</i><div>Q&amp;A / Planner</div></div><div class="architecture-grid"><article><span class="kicker">DETERMINISTIC</span><h3>Repository facts</h3><p>Structure, dependencies, changes, architecture signals, and other repository-derived information form the evidence layer.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">GROUNDED</span><h3>Traceable answers</h3><p>Higher-level outputs can reference evidence rather than presenting unsupported repository claims.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">ACTIONABLE</span><h3>Engineering plans</h3><p>The planner turns grounded context into structured implementation and verification steps.</p></article></div></section>

  <section id="demo" class="section container demo-section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">03 / PROOF</span><h2>See the shape of an engineering decision.</h2><p>The production website uses generated sample artifacts so the experience remains static, reproducible, and honest about what GitHub Pages can execute.</p></div><div class="evidence-card"><div class="evidence-header"><span>CHANGE PROOF</span><span class="status">GROUNDED</span></div><div class="evidence-body"><div><small>CHANGE</small><strong>PaymentService</strong></div><div><small>AFFECTED</small><strong>3 components · 6 test candidates</strong></div><div><small>EVIDENCE</small><strong>E17 · E21 · E34</strong></div><div><small>UNCERTAINTY</small><strong>Runtime gateway behaviour requires integration verification.</strong></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="cta container"><div><span class="kicker">OPEN SOURCE</span><h2>Explore the implementation.</h2><p>Read the code, run CodeContext, inspect the documentation, and contribute.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/CodeContext">Open repository ↗</a></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.hero{padding:112px 0 40px;position:relative}.hero::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0 -30vw auto;height:520px;z-index:-1;background:radial-gradient(circle at 50% 30%,rgb(115 213 255 / 10%),transparent 48%);pointer-events:none}.eyebrow,.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.eyebrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;margin-bottom:26px}.pulse{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--success);box-shadow:0 0 14px rgb(110 231 183 / 70%)}h1{max-width:900px;margin:0;font-size:clamp(3.2rem,8vw,6.8rem);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.065em}h1 span{color:var(--muted)}.hero-copy{max-width:700px;margin:30px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.25rem)}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.button{display:inline-flex;min-height:44px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:0 18px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:650;font-size:.9rem;transition:transform .18s ease,border-color .18s ease}.button:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}.primary{background:var(--text);color:var(--bg)}.secondary{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel)}.terminal{margin-top:72px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:#080c12;box-shadow:0 30px 80px rgb(0 0 0 / 30%);overflow:hidden}.terminal-bar{height:42px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:0 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font:.72rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.terminal-bar span{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--line)}.terminal-bar strong{margin-left:8px;font-weight:500}pre{margin:0;padding:28px;overflow-x:auto;color:#cbd5e1;font:.82rem/1.8 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.dim{color:var(--muted)}.ok{color:var(--success)}.warn{color:#fbbf24}.accent{color:var(--accent)}.section{padding-top:120px}.section-heading{max-width:800px;margin-bottom:42px}.section-heading h2,.cta h2{margin:10px 0;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.04em}.section-heading p,.cta p{color:var(--muted);max-width:680px}.capability-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px}.capability-card,.architecture-grid article,.evidence-card{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);border-radius:10px}.capability-card{min-height:190px;padding:22px}.index{color:var(--muted);font:.72rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}h3{margin:28px 0 8px;font-size:1rem}.capability-card p,.architecture-grid p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem}.flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:32px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);border-radius:10px;font:.82rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.flow div{padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;background:var(--panel-2)}.flow i{color:var(--accent);font-style:normal}.architecture-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin-top:10px}.architecture-grid article{padding:24px}.architecture-grid h3{margin-top:18px}.demo-section{padding-bottom:20px}.evidence-card{overflow:hidden}.evidence-header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:14px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font:600 .7rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.status{color:var(--success)}.evidence-body{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line)}.evidence-body>div{padding:24px;background:var(--panel)}.evidence-body small{display:block;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--muted);font:.68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.evidence-body strong{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:550}.cta{margin-top:120px;padding:38px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,var(--panel),#0b1018)}
@media(max-width:1000px){h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,5.4rem)}.capability-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.architecture-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.architecture-grid article:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}}
@media(max-width:700px){.hero{padding-top:78px}.section{padding-top:88px}.capability-grid,.architecture-grid,.evidence-body{grid-template-columns:1fr}.architecture-grid article:last-child{grid-column:auto}.flow{justify-content:flex-start;overflow-x:auto;flex-wrap:nowrap;scrollbar-width:thin;padding:20px}.flow i{flex:0 0 auto}.cta{margin-top:88px;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;padding:26px}.terminal{margin-top:48px}.terminal-bar{padding-inline:12px}pre{padding:20px;font-size:.74rem}.hero-copy{margin-block:22px}.actions{width:100%}.actions .button{flex:1 1 180px}}
@media(max-width:430px){h1{font-size:clamp(2.55rem,14vw,3.5rem)}.container{width:calc(100% - 24px)}.section-heading h2,.cta h2{font-size:2rem}.capability-card,.architecture-grid article,.evidence-body>div{padding:20px}.button{width:100%}.evidence-header{padding-inline:14px}.hero{padding-top:64px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.button{transition:none}}
</style>
